From: cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: reserve the hole between xbl and aop

Downstream reserves 0x85d00000..0x85f40000 as one contiguous block
(xbl_dump_mem plus xbl_aop_mem). Mainline covers xbl_mem, which ends at
0x85e40000, and aop_mem, which starts at 0x85f00000: that leaves 768 KB
unreserved in between, which the kernel hands out as normal memory.

The AOP manages the RPMh resources, among them the clocks and the RF power,
so corrupting its memory can show up very far away.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
@@ -98,6 +98,21 @@
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * Downstream reserves 0x85d00000..0x85f40000 in one go for XBL
+		 * and AOP. Mainline only covers xbl_mem (up to 0x85e40000) and
+		 * aop_mem (from 0x85f00000), leaving 768 KB loose in between
+		 * that Linux ends up using as ordinary memory.
+		 *
+		 * The AOP manages the RPMh resources, RF clocks and power
+		 * included, so trampling its memory can break things very far
+		 * from where it shows.
+		 */
+		xbl_aop_hole: memory@85e40000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x85e40000 0x0 0xc0000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		tz_mem: memory@86200000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x86200000 0x0 0x5500000>;
 			no-map;
